WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.934
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.069
We're here with
Allison Williams.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.371
So even before this film
came out, "M3GAN" became

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.541
this sort of iconic image,
very meme-able.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:12.344
But for you, how often were you
acting with a person?

00:00:12.344 --> 00:00:13.847
How often was it CGI?

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.482
Were there puppets involved?

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.383
-Well, I love the way you ask
it, like,

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.485
that couldn't --
Yes, there were.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:22.054
So, I didn't want to talk about
it too much before the movie

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.624
came out because the magic is
kind of like I just want people

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.159
to think of her as M3gan.
But that aside, just because

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:28.594
it's fun to discuss,

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.329
we achieved her in a couple of
different ways.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:33.532
One was just like a static,
posable doll that didn't do

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.302
anything but was terrifying.
I think the scariest of all.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.472
-Of all of them, the static one?
-I think so because also she was

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:43.442
most likely to be sort of be
left in a corner somewhere.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:45.545
And so then you're likely to be
running to the bathroom,

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.247
like gotta run, and then you run
past, like, she's just there.

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:50.249
[ Laughter ]
So she was the scariest.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.485
Then there was an animatronic
which required,

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.886
I think, six people to operate.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:56.255
-There was a puppeteer, a grip
usually moving her around,

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:59.025
two people on these what looked
like video game controllers.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.359
I think they weren't.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:03.062
Who were like making her face
move and making her blink

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.565
and stuff like that, and then
a guy at a switchboard

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.966
who was controlling her audio

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.602
and the actual mechanisms
that made her work.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.004
And that was
the most complicated.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.507
She was very temperamental,
the animatronic.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.409
And then there was Amie.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.747
So, Amie was 12 when we made the
movie, and she performed M3gan

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.416
in the more -- like when she
danced, for example,

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.717
that was Amie.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:28.320
And she gets -- Mm, she runs
in a very specific way

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.990
through the forest at one point,
and that was also Amie.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.594
And that was also terrifying,
though, because in -- So, Amie

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.163
is like, if you could put
sunshine in a person,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.264
like, that is Amie.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.834
She is so joyful and sweet.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.468
But the mask is terrifying.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.571
So when you look at her,
I had to tell myself,

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.005
like, she's smiling
under the mask.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.507
she's smiling under the mask,
she's smiling under the mask

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.341
because it was just
like a dead stare.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:52.245
Plus, they had tiny pinholes
in her eyes

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.713
so that she could see out.
[ Audience gasps ]

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.615
Not in her eyes.
We didn't torture this child.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.616
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.217
That came out wrong.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:00.887
-They cut tiny little holes in
the mask, in the eyeballs

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.088
of the mask so she could see
out, but they fogged up.

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:05.157
So she could only see
for about five minutes,

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:07.627
and then she was just like
unable to see anything.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.928
She couldn't hear very easily,

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.697
so she communicated
with hand signals.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.498
So you're interacting with
this being

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.001
that's going like this all day,
or this, or this.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.569
And then the mask comes off,
and she's like --

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.239
[ Breathing heavily ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:22.375
-Was part of her audition to run
with a mask through the woods?

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.476
-I mean no,
but it should have been.

00:02:24.476 --> 00:02:26.179
I just want to see
a whole reality show.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.581
If they make like, "Is this
cake?", they should also

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.716
just make that into a show.
-Is this puppet?

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:33.052
-Yeah, exactly.
-Is this Amie? Is this puppet?

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.954
-Exactly. But it was really hard
to tell the difference

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.889
between all three of them.
Even when you see them

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:38.390
next to each other, which I
have, I think,

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.593
a photo of all three of them.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.127
Oh, this is so --
Oh, wow, these are all three.

00:02:42.127 --> 00:02:43.896
-Yes. So that's all three.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.465
-Oh, I would have no idea.
-I want you to try to guess.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:50.903
-Okay. Um, uh, uh...

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:52.104
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:53.873
That's the -- That's the doll.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.441
That's Amie.
That's the animatronic.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.109
-No.
-Okay.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.511
-Should I just leave it at that?
-Yeah.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.714
-Great.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.349
That's so annoying.
-You're very good.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.917
You're a very good
executive producer.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.752
-Thank you!
-"I'm not going to give away
the answer."

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.688
-No. But you were wrong,
which is amazing.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.056
So it was like -- Yeah.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.757
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:13.158
-No, wait a second.

00:03:13.158 --> 00:03:14.560
She said, "It's amazing that
someone like me could be wrong."

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.163
-It never happens.
It's never happened.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.264
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.265
Alexi paid me good money
to make you wrong.

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:23.069
-Oh, my God, yeah.
Alexi manages to find a few.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.370
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.805
We love her.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:28.775
So, yeah, it was like a really
creepy -- The experience of

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:31.076
filming it was creepiest when we
weren't actually rolling

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:33.913
because then -- But having that
this close to you,

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.448
as you just saw in the clip,
like, it's intense.

00:03:36.448 --> 00:03:39.252
It's a lot. It felt human too.
That's the creepiest part.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.886
-Well, I mean, I think that's
one of the reasons

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:43.089
people are responding to it
again.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:46.726
All of a sudden, you see a
character in a horror movie

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.361
that is unlike any one
you've seen before,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.596
and it's just really fun.
It's inventive and cool.

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:52.031
You're great in it.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.600
Congratulations both on starring
in it and executive producing

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.803
it, and it is always so
wonderful to have you here.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.237
-Thank you for having me.
-I hope everybody sees it.

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.906
I know it had
a big first weekend.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.909
But go check out "M3GAN"
in theaters.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.378
We'll be right back with
S.S. Rajamouli.

